title: Carl Ultizka withdraws from the Zentrum chairmanship.
subtitle: The Right pushes out the Center Party's Clerical left
view-if: year = 1928 and month = 9 and z_party_leader = "Marx"
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true

= Center Party Conference

Previously, Carl Ulitzka, a member of Zentrum Left, was set to be the Clerical Wing's candidate for Zentrum leadership, but, the Right of people like Franz von Papen has got him to resign

The consensus candidate on the right is Ludwig Kaas, a Catholic priest who represents the party's traditionalists. He will be the wing's candidate if we do not interevene, but we may be able to force Ulitzka back into the race.

- @kaas: The Center Party nominates Ludwig Kaas as the party chair.
- @left: Influence the Clerical Wing to nominate Ulitzka.

@kaas

Ludwig Kaas has been selected as the chairman of the Center Party. He seems to represent a rightward turn from Marx, and will preside over a Center Party less inclined to compromise with the left.

@left
unavailable-subtitle: Our relations are not good enough.
subtitle: Ulitzka is likely to be friendlier to us than Kaas.
choose-if: z_relation >= 60
on-arrival: Q.ulitzka = 1; workers_z += 3

With our grassroots connections, we have been able to influence the Center delegates to support Carl Ulitzka as the new Center chairman. He is more too the left than Kaas, and will be more inclined to collaborate with us compared to him.
